068 #edb/ref 17592186433398 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433399 1069 "q-64274" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433399 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433399 1071 "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4y=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433399 1072 #uuid "1961edb1-4065-5e30-966d-35cef05a7365" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433399 1074 "The particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n4(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+4x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-4\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+4\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\ -4\\alpha =-4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =0.$ Therefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433397 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1069 "q-64273" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1071 "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1072 #uuid "9012ef7a-2685-5e88-afc5-3c045fe01d15" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433400 1074 "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha -\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(\\alpha -3\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha -\\beta =10\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ \\alpha -3\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-3$ and $\\beta =-1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433396 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1069 "q-8121" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1071 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1072 #uuid "ac410cb2-42ca-5768-b913-c9a0282fb269" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true] [17592186433401 1074 "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=0\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-1\\pm 2\\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+5(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n(4\\alpha +2\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(-2\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha +2\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\ -2\\alpha +4\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$" 13194139534704 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1c44fa17-bdc5-51f4-a438-7e8acea31ae7" 17592186433381 "answer-23ff9445-e0ef-5464-9534-037aa0779f66" 17592186433382 "answer-242d2d52-f50c-5e80-9ccb-b96c31a527b3" 17592186433383 "answer-2dba37db-2930-5acd-8ac5-1cb53904e50c" 17592186433384 "answer-35e4d2e5-706c-5258-9456-9e4bb7705e64" 17592186433385 "answer-3ae0d677-84f2-52e7-8b0c-cac1d9bc44ce" 17592186433386 "answer-444f2f73-423e-52cf-8993-630d12d4bc82" 17592186433387 "answer-57a9a361-15d8-51a5-8e9b-65d82be746f1" 17592186433388 "answer-5ab46f34-d8f7-59d6-bdbd-52cb67a2e827" 17592186433389 "answer-a2852e49-1123-5dbc-9513-0f9543e796a2" 17592186433390 "answer-a9935964-0a92-5948-9e9b-226df2fc5db4" 17592186433391 "answer-ced8ae93-61ba-5589-ac22-bbbff77d9eef" 17592186433392 "answer-e6867f40-4226-51fd-bc11-e7fdeae8d0a4" 17592186433393 "answer-e8bccbd1-e170-5521-a778-3b5dc8e5cf86" 17592186433394 "answer-e916876a-ab3b-5e56-a063-0f250160ca0c" 17592186433395 "answer-field-73960a55-87e7-51f7-88d8-3235589147ec" 17592186433396 "answer-field-7437ed1b-b3b5-570b-9f04-43fb6c608cb0" 17592186433397 "answer-field-d0af414f-f694-5afc-9853-4520f38d8893" 17592186433398 "question-1961edb1-4065-5e30-966d-35cef05a7365" 17592186433399 "question-9012ef7a-2685-5e88-afc5-3c045fe01d15" 17592186433400 "question-ac410cb2-42ca-5768-b913-c9a0282fb269" 17592186433401}}
